[size=4][b]Prerequisites[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Venworks Canvas and Venworks Core Library 2.1.8 or later installed as authoring masters.
[*]A Starfield plugin editor that can create the quest and bind script properties.
[*]The Starfield Papyrus compiler with the Starfield, Venworks Core, and Canvas script sources available.
[*]An ActionScript 3 compiler compatible with the repository's Apache Flex and Player 11.1 build target.
[*]Archive2 or another packaging workflow that preserves the paths in this guide.
[*]A new or disposable PC save for the first in-game test.
[/list]

[size=4][b]1. Choose permanent identities[/b][/size]

Choose these values before creating records or files. They must agree across the ESM, Papyrus properties, SWF registration, and packaged paths.

[table]
[tr]
[td][b]Identity[/b][/td]
[td][b]Example used in this guide[/b][/td]
[td][b]Rule[/b][/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]Plugin file[/td]
[td]Acme-Canvas-Example.esm[/td]
[td]Use a unique filename and do not rename it after release without a migration plan.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]Papyrus namespace[/td]
[td]Acme:CanvasExample[/td]
[td]Keep every compiled script for this plugin under the same namespace.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]Asset namespace[/td]
[td]acme.canvas-example[/td]
[td]Use lowercase ASCII letters, digits, dots, and hyphens. This becomes part of the Interface path.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]Consumer UUID[/td]
[td]your-generated-uuid[/td]
[td]Generate a new UUID once. Never reuse the UUID from the shipped Example or Gallery.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]Display name[/td]
[td]Acme Canvas Example[/td]
[td]This is the readable name Canvas reports in diagnostics.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]Descriptor version[/td]
[td]1[/td]
[td]Increase it when an installed update must replace the registered movie descriptor.[/td]
[/tr]
[/table]

[size=4][b]2. Create the HTML panel[/b][/size]

Create index.html and panel.css in a local resource folder. This starter displays complete data supplied by the Scaleform consumer; HTML does not read game data by itself.

[code-html]
<!doctype html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Acme Canvas Example</title>
    <meta charset="utf-8"></meta>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="panel.css"></link>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="panel">
      <h1>PLAYER STATUS</h1>
      <p data-vw-template="{playername} | LEVEL {playerlevel:integer}"></p>
      <p data-vw-template="HEALTH {health:integer}/{maxhealth:integer}"></p>
      <vw-meter class="health-meter" value="healthpercent"></vw-meter>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
[/code-html]

[code-css]
.panel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; width: 460px; margin: 28px 32px; padding: 14px; gap: 8px; color: #e3fdff; background-color: #141414d1; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid; border-color: #3aadfc; font-family: $MAIN_Font_Bold; font-size: 18px; line-height: 26px; }
.panel h1 { margin: 0px; color: #66ffff; font-size: 24px; line-height: 30px; }
.panel p { margin: 0px; }
.health-meter { width: 420px; height: 14px; color: #66ffff; background-color: #26313a; }
[/code-css]

[size=4][b]3. Create the Scaleform consumer[/b][/size]

The SWF is the adapter between Canvas and your document. It declares the data it needs, keeps a complete view model, and gives that model to the HTML bridge.

Your registration should have this shape:

[code-actionscript]
public function getCanvasRegistration() : Object
{
   return {
      "protocol":"VWCANVAS_CONSUMER/3",
      "consumerId":"your-generated-uuid",
      "assetNamespace":"acme.canvas-example",
      "version":1,
      "minimumContractVersion":3,
      "maximumContractVersion":3,
      "hostKinds":["player"],
      "uiChannels":["PlayerData","PlayerFrequentData"],
      "eventSubscriptions":[],
      "marker":"ACME_CANVAS_EXAMPLE"
   };
}

public function getCanvasHtmlRegistration() : Object
{
   return {"contract":"VWCANVAS_HTML/2","entryDocument":"index.html"};
}
[/code-actionscript]

Canvas calls three fixed callbacks on a current consumer:

[table]
[tr]
[td][b]Callback[/b][/td]
[td][b]What your SWF should do[/b][/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]handleUIData(channel, data)[/td]
[td]Copy only validated values from a requested game UI channel into your saved view model, then publish the complete model.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]handleCanvasEvent(topic, body)[/td]
[td]Decode and validate a subscribed Canvas datagram, commit the complete accepted update, then publish. Leave the previous valid model unchanged when validation fails.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]handleLifecycle(state, detail)[/td]
[td]On ready, obtain the HTML bridge, set the viewport, and publish the initial model. On unload, release the bridge and any timers or listeners.[/td]
[/tr]
[/table]

[size=4][b]4. Build the consumer movie[/b][/size]

Compile the document class as an ActionScript 3 movie targeting the same Player 11.1 runtime as Canvas. Your build must produce a consumer movie, not a second Canvas host. Do not embed Canvas's HTML parser, renderer, subscription manager, or host classes in the consumer SWF.

[size=4][b]5. Create the Papyrus registrar[/b][/size]

Create a Start Game Enabled quest and attach a registrar script that extends Venworks:Canvas:Base:BaseQuest.

Bind these quest properties:

[table]
[tr]
[td][b]Property[/b][/td]
[td][b]Value for this guide[/b][/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]Registry[/td]
[td]The VWCANVAS_Registry quest from Venworks-Canvas.esm[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]ConsumerId[/td]
[td]Your permanent UUID[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]DisplayName[/td]
[td]Acme Canvas Example[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]NormalMoviePath[/td]
[td]VenworksCanvas/Consumers/acme.canvas-example/normal.swf[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]LargeMoviePath[/td]
[td]VenworksCanvas/Consumers/acme.canvas-example/large.swf[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]DescriptorVersion[/td]
[td]1[/td]
[/tr]
[tr]
[td]ExpectedRegistration[/td]
[td]True[/td]
[/tr]
[/table]

[size=4][b]6. Add mod-owned data[/b][/size]

Use Canvas UI channels for data already supplied by the game UI. Use Canvas datagrams for a complete state or occurrence produced by your Papyrus code.

[code-papyrus]
OperationResult result = Registry.TryPublishCanvasDatagram(
  "acme.canvas-example.status",
  "panel.state",
  1,
  "ci-ascii",
  "ready|42"
)
Registry.LogOperation(result)
[/code-papyrus]

[size=4][b]7. Author the ESM[/b][/size]

Create a light master with these masters:
[list]
[*]Starfield.esm
[*]Venworks-Core.esm
[*]Venworks-Canvas.esm
[/list]

Add one quest, mark it Start Game Enabled and Starts Enabled, attach your compiled registrar, and fill every mandatory property.

[size=4][b]8. Package the files[/b][/size]

The installed layout must resolve to these paths:

[code]
Data/
  Acme-Canvas-Example.esm
  Acme-Canvas-Example - Main.ba2

Acme-Canvas-Example - Main.ba2
  Scripts/Acme/CanvasExample/Registrar.pex
  Interface/VenworksCanvas/Consumers/acme.canvas-example/normal.swf
  Interface/VenworksCanvas/Consumers/acme.canvas-example/large.swf
  Interface/VenworksCanvas/Consumers/acme.canvas-example/index.html
  Interface/VenworksCanvas/Consumers/acme.canvas-example/panel.css
[/code]

[size=4][b]9. Test in increasing scope[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Inspect the ESM after saving.
[*]Compile the registrar with no Papyrus errors.
[*]Compile the SWF and confirm the movie contains your own UUID and namespace.
[*]Inspect the BA2 and confirm every file uses the exact packaged path.
[*]Install Canvas plus only your add-on on a disposable save.
[*]Open the Player HUD and confirm the initial HTML appears.
[*]Change or trigger each data source and confirm the visible values update.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Common mistakes[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Reusing the shipped Example or Gallery UUID.
[*]Letting the ESM UUID, SWF UUID, namespace, movie paths, or descriptor version disagree.
[*]Expecting HTML bindings to read game state without the consumer calling setData().
[*]Sending partial setData() objects and accidentally removing earlier values.
[*]Treating ci-ascii payload text as case preserving.
[*]Using one topic for both current state and replayable occurrences.
[*]Loading remote assets, JavaScript, browser APIs, forms, navigation, or unsupported CSS.
[*]Packaging a second copy of Canvas host classes inside the consumer SWF.
[/list]
